# Potts, letter Ci - Cl

Cicero.; Cicero.

@HH 322. There was one with me... it was given to believe that it was Cicero. His views on wisdom, order, the Word, and the Lord. @SE 4094. @4415.

@DSS 115[3]. Source of Cicero's knowledge about spiritual things.

Cinder. See <Ashes>.

Cineritious.; Cineritius.

@AC 6607. The cineritious substance in the brain. @DLW 316[3]. @TCR 351[3].

Cinnamon.; Cinnamomum.

@AC 10254. "Aromatic cinnamon" (Exodus 30:23) = the perception and affection of natural truth. Explained. @10264[2]. @AR 777. @--[end].

@AE 1150. "Cinnamon" = the good of celestial love. Explained.

Circle.; Circulus. See <Gyre>.

@AC 814[end]. To distinguish them they have a kind of circle with brass points... @SE 1280.

@3869[2]. Such is the circle of things with men. @4247[2].

@--[3]. @WE 970. @SE 757, Explained.

@4658[4]. The radiant circle is the Divine from Him.

@5017[end]. The circle by what communications take place.

@7173. The Lord seen encompassed with a solar circle.

@9407[14]. The light which is the Divine truth proceeding from the Lord was described by radiant circles... @DLW 94.

@10057[2]. Such is the circle of things from the world through the natural man into his spiritual man, and from this again into the world. Explained.

@--[3]. As this circle is the circle of man's life...

@10188[2]. This Divine sphere was likened to radiant circles...

@DP 29[3]. Such a circle of the love to the thoughts and from the thoughts to the love from the love is in all things of the human mind; which circle may be called the circle of life. See @SE 757.

@335[3]. Comparison with squaring the circle.

@CL 249. The mind is thus circumscribed as in a circle...

@269[3]. Such a man appears from Heaven... with a yellow circle round the head; such a one... with a white circle. The circles round the head represent intelligence. Explained.

@--[4]. A devil seen rising up with a lucid white circle round his head...

@TCR 365[3]. The Sun is the nearest circle...

@756. This is called the circle of things...

@SE 3484. Forms which far surpass the circle and the curves which relate to the circle.

@AE 242[4]. The circle of man's life is to know, to understand, to will, and to do...

@543[12]. "Jehovah Who dwells upon the circle of the earth" (Isaiah 40:22) = that the Lord as to intelligence is in the highest things.

@799[15]. To "dwell upon the circle of the earth" = upon Heaven, for Heaven encompasses the earth as a circle does its centre.

@DLove 10[2]. All love returns as by a circle to that from which it came.

@DWis 12[end]. Angelic Idea of Creation. The Divine which proceeds was effigied by golden or lucid circles round the head of God.

Circuit.; Circuitus. Circuitio.

@AC 2936[end]. This outermost is called the circuit.

@2973[2]. In the Word are mentioned "the midst" and "the circuit." When Canaan is treated of... "the circuit" was where the surrounding nations were.

@--[3]. "The circuit" = what is outermost.

@--[4]. With man... from the inmost the Lord rules those things which are in his circuits; and when man suffers the Lord to dispose the circuits to correspondence with the inmost things, he is in a state in which he can receive Heaven... But when the man does not suffer the Lord to dispose the circuits to correspondence, the man recedes from Heaven in the same proportion.

@--. The body is in the circuit...

@6607. Circuits -circuitus- in the brain.

@8870[3]. Those who are in the circuits of Heaven...

@SE 2438. On the circuit of evil. @2776.

@AE 269. "A rainbow round about the throne" (Revelation 4:3) = Divine truth round about.

@283. "Six wings about him" (Revelation 4:8) = the Divine Spiritual around it.

@340[12]. "The circuit" (Ezekiel 34:26) = that which is outside or below.

@449[5]. "The circuits of Jerusalem" (Jeremiah 17:26) = truths of doctrine in the natural man.

@644[14]. "The circuits of the hill of Jehovah" (Ezekiel 34:26) = all who are in truths of doctrine and thence in the good of charity.

@650[46]. "Gathered from every side" (Ezekiel 39:17) = all in whatever state...

@695[25]. "From every side" (Ezekiel 16:33) = from everywhere.

Circulate.; Circulare.
Circulation.; Circulatio.

@AC 6607. Thoughts with affections... circulate almost according to the form of the circumvolutions of the cineritious substance in the human brain...

@6944. The long dispute about the circulation of the blood.

@CL 78[8]. It decreased according to the circulation.

@TCR 577[2]. Thence is the circulation (of the blood).

Circumcise.; Circumcidere.
Circumcision.; Circumcisio.
See <Foreskin>.

@AC 1025[5]. Circumcision was the covenant here treated of, by which is meant circumcision of the heart, which is that of those who are in love; circumcision was a representative of regeneration through love. Illustrated.

@--. Wherefore wherever "circumcision" is mentioned, nothing else is meant than love and charity, and thence life.

@1038[7]. Why the sabbath and circumcision are called "signs of the covenant." Illustrated.

@1986. That man must first remove loves and their filthy cupidities, and thus be purified, is what is represented by circumcision.

@2039. "Every male to be circumcised" (Genesis 17:10) = purity... Circumcision, or the cutting off of the foreskin, signified the removal of those things which hinder and defile heavenly love, and which are evils of cupidities, especially of the cupidities of self-love, and the falsities thence. Explained.

@--[2]. That circumcision is only a sign of a covenant or of conjunction, is evident from the fact, that the circumcision of the foreskin is nothing at all without the circumcision of the heart; and that it is the circumcision of the heart, which is purification from those filthy loves, which is signified. Illustrated. @6804[11].

@--[7]. When the Angels have the idea of purification from filthy natural things, with extreme rapidity there is represented something like circumcision in the World of Spirits... They with whom this rapid circumcision was represented in the World of Spirits were wanting to be admitted into Heaven, and before they were admitted this was represented. Hence it is evident why command was given to Joshua that the people should be circumcised, when having crossed the Jordan, they were entering Canaan. (Joshua 5).

@2041. "Ye shall circumcise the flesh of your foreskin" (Genesis 17:11) = the removal of the love of self and of the world. "Circumcision" = purification from filthy loves. @2042. @2044. @2045.

@2051. "Circumcising shall be circumcised" (Genesis 17:13) = that they shall completely remove from themselves the loves of self and of the world... "Circumcision" = purification from the loves of self and of the world.

@2057. "He who is not circumcised in the flesh of his foreskin" (Genesis 17:14) = him who is in self-love. Explained.

@2102. "He circumcised the flesh of their foreskin" (Genesis 17:23) = their purification and righteousness from the Lord. To be "circumcised" = to be purified from the loves of self and of the world.

@2107. "In his circumcising the flesh of bis foreskin" (Genesis 17:24) = when He entirely expelled the evils of the external man. To be "circumcised" = to be purified from the loves of self and of the world, or what is the same, from evils, for all evils are thence. @2110.

@2112. "Abraham was circumcised, and Ishmael his son" (Genesis 17:26) = that when the Lord conjoined His human essence with His Divine essence, He also conjoined with Himself all others who become rational by truth, and saved them... To be "circumcised" = to be purified, and when predicated of the Lord, = to be glorified.

@2116. "They were circumcised by him" (Genesis 17:27) = that they were justified by the Lord. To be "circumcised" = to be purified.

@2632. "Abraham circumcised Isaac his son" (Genesis 21:4) = the purification of the Rational.

@--[2]. Circumcision in the Ancient Church represented that man was to be purified from the loves of self and of the world... @2634. @2799[6].

@4462. The word circumcision was used to distinguish between those who were of the Church and those who were not, for circumcision = recession from filthy loves... and accession to heavenly loves... thus accession to the Church.

@--[2]. The Most Ancient Church knew nothing of circumcision, but only the Ancient Church; from this Church circumcision emanated to many nations, and was enjoined on Abraham and his descendants not as anything new... and became to them a sign that they were of the Church... Circumcision, however, was only a sign representative of purification from the love of self and of the world; on being purified from which they are spiritually circumcised, and are said to be circumcised as to the heart. Illustrated.

@4486. "In the circumcising of every male, as they are circumcised" (Genesis 34:22) = if they were initiated thereby in the representatives of these things as to mere externals. To be "circumcised" = an external representative, a sign that they were of the Church.

@4489[end]. Hamor and Shechem sinned enormously in receiving circumcision. Explained.

@4493. "They circumcised every male, all that went out of the gate of his city" (Genesis 34:24) = accession to external things.

@4496. The "pain" after circumcision = cupidity. Explained.

@7044. The reason circumcision was done with knives of stone = that purification from filthy loves should be effected through truths of faith. Explained. @9088[2]. @AE 701[25].

@7049. "A bridegroom of bloods for the circumcisions" (Exodus 4:26) = that although the internal was full of violence and hostility to truth and good, still circumcision was to be received as a sign representative of purification from filthy loves. @8000.

@8009. "Let all his males be circumcised" (Exodus 12:48) = that his truth is to be purified from impure loves.

@9088[2]. Circumcision signified purification from these filthy loves.

@9272[4]. Wherefore it is said that they should "circumcise themselves to Jehovah, and remove the foreskins of the heart" (Jeremiah 4:4), that is, that they should purify themselves from such things as suffocate or render unfruitful the truths and goods of faith. References.

@DFaith 51. By those who are circumcised are meant those who are in spiritual love.

@54. That by "circumcision" was represented purification from the evils which are of merely natural love, is evident from these passages. Illustrated.

@--. To "circumcise the heart" or "the foreskin of the heart" (Jeremiah 4:4, Deuteronomy 10:16) = to purify themselves from evils.

@TCR 674. Baptism was instituted in place of circumcision, because by the circumcision of the foreskin was represented the circumcision of the heart... General article.

@--. The primary thing which distinguished the Israelitish Church from the other Churches in the Asiatic world, and afterwards from the Christian Church, was circumcision.

@--. Circumcision signified the rejection of the concupiscences of the flesh, and thus purification from evils... @675[2], Illustrated.

@675. That circumcision was instituted as a sign that the men of the Israelitish Church were of the posterity of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. Illustrated.

@AE 109[6]. As fruits signified the goods of life with man... it was commanded that the fruits of trees... should be circumcised (Leviticus 19:23, 24, 25).

@709[23]. The reason a covenant was made by circumcision, was that circumcision represented purification from the loves of self and of the world, which are corporeal and earthly loves, and their removal.

Circumference.; Circumferentia.

@AC 1624. A very bright light encompassed with a kind of circumference...

@1625. At the circumference...

@5291[10]. The number of the circumference does not answer geometrically to the diameter, yet spiritually it involves that which is signified by the compass of that vessel.

@TCR 268[end]. The nations in Asia and the Indies constitute the last circumference.

Circumference.; Peripheria. Peripheries.

@AC 2657[3]. The things which do not agree... are rejected as it were to the circumference.

@2940. Those things which are not good are presented at the circumference.

@3089. At last falsities and evils are removed, and are cast as it were into the circumference...

@3436[end]. Falsities are thus withheld as it were in the circumferences... But with those who are not in the good of life... truths hold the circuits, or circumferences. @4552[2].

@3833[2]. Man then proceeds from the good and truth which he believes and perceives, as from the centre to the circumferences... And then, as from new centres, he brings forth new circumferences.

@3993[12]. Deceit... sets evil in the midst, and rejects good to the circumferences.

@--[13]. The evils with which goods are mingled, and the falsities with which truths are mingled, are wonderfully disposed into order by the Lord... so that goods with truths are in the midst, and by degrees towards the circuits or circumferences, are such evils and falsities.

@4482[3]. They who are in a like degree of good are also in a like degree of truth, and are thus as it were at a like distance, or, so to speak, at the same circumference. Hence "breadth" is predicated of truths.

@4552[2]. Fallacious truths are at the exterior circumferences... The outermost circumferences are the lowest things of the Natural.

@4564[2]. Both hereditary and actual evil... are only separated, and through disposition by the Lord, rejected into the circumferences. Explained. @5134[2].

@5530. The truths with man are disposed in series... Those which do not at all agree with the loves, are rejected to the last circumferences.

@6084[2]. What is kept directly before the sight is in the the centre... the rest are around in the circumferences...

@6451[2]. Exterior things make the circumferences...

@6604[end]. Then the rest of the Societies are, for him, at the circumferences.

@7542[2]. In the other life, these things are evolved according to the order in which they have been arranged; first come forth those things which hold the last circumferences...

@DP 79[2]. These goods... remove evils towards the circumferences, further and further, according to the aversion for them...

@86. Thus the goods in the circumferences with the evil are defiled by the evils of the centre; and the evils in the circumferences with the good are made mild by the goods of the centre.

@TCR 214. Simultaneous order is like a work cohering with the circumferences from the centre even to the last surface.

@DWis 12. 5. 3. The Sun of Heaven is the common centre of the universe, and all things of it are circumferences and circumferences even to the last one...

Circumgyrate.; Circumgyrare.
Circumgyration.; Circumgyratio.

@AC 2602. The universe, which they believe to circumgyrate...

@8812[4]. The sun of Heaven... does not produce these states by any circumgyration. @7381[4].

@DLW 270[end]. An evil Spirit cannot circumgyrate his body from left to right, but from right to left; but a good Spirit can with difficulty circumgyrate his body from right to left, but easily from left to right. The circumgyration follows the flux of the interiors which are of the mind.

@SE 155[4]. I have been able to feel such circumgyrations... upon me...

@4298. They were punished by... circumgyration. Described.

Circumrotate.; Circumrotare.
Circumrotation.; Circumrotatio.

@AC 829. Their punishment is... that they are circumrotated rapidly like a roll, from left to right... @5188[2]. @SE 1485. @1806. @4309. @4714.

@6110[4]. The earth, by its circumrotation, turns itself from the sun...

@SE 1183. They are beautifully circumrotated...

@1259[2]. There, sitting on a seat, he was circumrotated, which signified that he was versatile.

@4087[end]. Hence come... bodily progressions, circumrotations, etc.

@4327. A new kind of punishment by circumrotation.

Circumspection.; Circumspectio.
To exercise Circumspection.; Circumspicere.

@AC 197. "A serpent," with the most ancients, signified circumspection...

@--. "The brazen serpent" = the Lord's Sensual... Who alone exercises circumspection and provides for all.

@3901[5]. The face of an eagle = circumspection, and thence Providence.

@6398[2]. The very sagacity and circumspection which comes forth in externals, is signified by "serpents."

@AR 561. The Divine circumspection for the New Church. Signified.

@CL 194. The innate circumspection of wives.

@AE 281[2]. "He placed it circumspectly" (Ezekiel 17:5) = multiplication... To "place it circumspectly" = to separate from falsities.

Circumstance.; Circumstantia.

@AC 2481. Describing... with many circumstances... @2482. @2483[end].

@7298[end]. According to circumstances.

@HH 462[8]. All the circumstances appear together.

@CL 166. It does not become me to open these things as to the circumstances.

@485. Circumstances... vary the case. @SE 60. @2537.

@487[end]. They cannot be judged from these circumstances...

@530. There are various circumstances in the world that mitigate... and that aggravate crimes.

@SE 622. They permitted him to punish according to the circumstances.

@3537. Although circumstances vary truths, they do not take them away. Example(s).

@4312. On those who inhere in general truth without application to circumstances. Example(s).

Circumvolution.; Circumvolutio.

@AC 4040. There appear in the brain... wonderful circumvolutions and gyres... @4041. @6607.

@7381[3]. By apparent circumvolutions the sun appears to make day and night...

@--[4]. But the Sun of Heaven... does not make circumgyrations and circumvolutions.

@SE 1664. He was revolved... @1696. @1763. @1806.

Circus.; Circus.

@HH 223. In the form of a circus.

@AR 484[7]. Lo, there was a circus, and in the middle of it a pulpit.

@655. I saw an amphitheatre erected in the form of a circus...

@--. I saw as it were bullocks, sheep, etc., let into the area of the circus...

@961. I saw the Angels standing in the form of a circus...

@CL 183. In the middle there was a grassy circus.

Cistern.; Cisterna.
See <Pit>.

@AC 5180. The latter and the former are they who belong to the province of the cistern and ducts of the chyle.

@DP 164[6]. As the chyle is carried through the mesentery and the lacteal vessels there into the receptacle...

@296[14]. The chyle conveyed through the thoracic duct from its receptacle in the mesentery...

@TCR 814. Thought is like a water-course, and the speech thence is like a cistern.

@AE 617[13]. "Cisterns dug" (Deuteronomy 6:11) = the interiors of the natural mind full of the Knowledges of good and truth.

@638[14]. "Cisterns cut out" (Deuteronomy 6:11) = all things of intelligence in the natural man, which are cognitions and scientifics.

Citizen.; Cives.

@AC 1121[end]. Such are received as citizens everywhere in the earth, as they are also in the other life.

@1125[end]. Like good citizens.

@8257[end]. This life causes a man to be a citizen of the world; the former, a citizen of Heaven.

@DLife 12. Through this good, and according to it, is man a citizen in the Spiritual World.

@DP 322[2]. The difference is that the latter is not only a good citizen of an earthly kingdom, but is also a good citizen of the heavenly kingdom; whereas the former is a good citizen of an earthly kingdom, but not of the heavenly kingdom.

Citron.; Citrus. @AC 8603[2]. @TCR 78. @94[2].

City.; Civitas.
See <City-Urbs>.

@AC 402. "The holy city," which is also called "the holy Jerusalem" = the Lord's Kingdom in universal, or in each person in particular. In like manner "the city," or "mount of Zion"; the latter = what is celestial of faith, the former, what is spiritual of faith. What is celestial and spiritual itself is also described by "cities," etc. Illustrated.

@--[3]. As the celestial and spiritual things of faith are represented by "a city," so all doctrinal things are signified by the cities of Judah and Israel...

@1530. "The city has no need of the sun."

@1532. "The holy city."

@2943[2]. Hence "the city of God," and "the holy city" = faith in the Lord.

@--. As "a city -urbs-," or "city" = faith...

@3272[3]. "The holy city" = the Lord's Spiritual Kingdom. @5044[8].

@4411. When this truth inflows into the first Heaven... it appears as a paradise, and elsewhere as a city containing palaces.

@4434[2]. "The holy city," and "the New Jerusalem" = the Church.

@--. "A city" = the truth of the Church. References.

@5297. The truths and goods with a man form as it were a city; hence the man himself, in whom is the Church, is called "the city of God."

@--. A house, with its chambers, etc., is a city in the least form.

@5321[9]. "The city which shall be inhabited for ever" (Jeremiah 17:25) is not Jerusalem, but is the Lord's Church, which is signified by Jerusalem.

@5427[2]. There appeared to me a great city...

@HH 184. Arranged in the form of a city.

@307[2]. "The city Jerusalem descending from God out of heaven" = its heavenly doctrine revealed by the Lord.

@LJ 27[2]. As men dwell in cities...

@--. As from a village into a great city...

@DLord 64. "The holy city" = the doctrine of Divine truth from the Lord.

@DLW 367[end]. As in a city, commonwealth, and kingdom...

@AR 489. "The holy city they shall tread under foot forty-two months" (Revelation 11:2) = that it will disperse all the truth of the Word until there is not anything remaining.

@--. "The holy city," or "city -urbs-" = means the holy Jerusalem... To "tread that city under foot" = to disperse the truths of its doctrine.

@CL 77[2]. An extensive and spacious city (of the copper age in Heaven). Described.

@SE 5792. The ascent is by means of stairs from one city into the other.

@AE 223. "The name of the city of my God" (Revelation 3:12) = the doctrine of the New Church.

@--. "The city of my God" = the doctrine of Divine truth. Explained.

City.; Urbs.

@AC 402. "The city" built by Cain (Genesis 4:17) = everything doctrinal and heretical thence. Wherever the name of any city occurs in the Word, it never signifies a city, but something doctrinal, or heretical; for the Angels are completely ignorant what a city is, or the name of any city; they never have any idea of a city, nor can have... but only perceive what they signify. Illustrated. @1187. @1191.

@793. "City" belongs to the class of spiritual expressions.

@940[2]. Cities in the Spiritual World. @941. @942.

@1191. "This city is that great one" (Genesis 10:12) = doctrinal things, that they prevailed... The reason it is called "a great city," is that all falsity of doctrine and of worship thence is derived into falsity of life.

@1259[4]. "Cities" = truths.

@1304. "Let us build us a city and a tower" (Genesis 11:4) = that they invented a doctrine and a worship.

@1305. "A city" = doctrine, or what is doctrinal, both genuine and heretical.

@1324. "They ceased to build the city" (Genesis 11:8) = that such doctrine was not received. "City" = doctrine.

@1358. At that time cities were families which dwelt together.

@1597. "Lot dwelt in the cities of the plain" (Genesis 13:12) = that the external man was in scientifics. "A city," or "cities" = doctrinal things, which in themselves are nothing but scientifics, when predicated of the external man separated from the internal. "Cities" = doctrinal things, both true and false.

@1626. The cities in Heaven described.

@1664[5]. "The city of praise and of joy" (Jeremiah 49:25) = the things which are of the Church.

@2252. "Peradventure there be fifty righteous in the midst of the city" (Genesis 18:24) = that truths maybe full of goods... "City" = truth. @2261. @2268.

@2268. The human mind as to truths is compared in the Word to "a city," and is also called "a city"; and as to the goods which are in the truths, it is compared to the inhabitants therein... Truths in the memory without goods, are like a city without inhabitants. @2712.

@2309. I saw little boys fighting in the streets of a great city... @HH 344.

@2346. "The men of the city" (Genesis 19:4) = those who are in falsities... "City" = truths, also falsities or things contrary to truths.

@2392. "Everyone who is in the city" (Genesis 19:12) = whatever derives anything from truth... "City" = what is doctrinal, thus truth in its complex.

@2408. "Lest thou be consumed in the iniquity of the city" (Genesis 19:15) = lest they perish in evils of falsity. "City" = what is doctrinal, false as well as true.

@2413. "They set him without the city" (Genesis 19:16) = away from falsity.

@2417. "Look not behind thee" (Genesis 19:17) = that he should not look to doctrinal things; for the city was behind him, and the mountain before him. "A city" = what is doctrinal. @2418.

@2418[end]. The doctrinal things of charity are called "the cities of the mountain," and the doctrinal things of faith, "the cities of the plain" (Jeremiah 33:13).

@2428. "This city is near to flee to" (Genesis 19:20) = that it was allowable from the truth of faith. "City" = what is doctrinal, thus the truth of faith. @2429. @2430. @2435.

@2449. "He overthrew those cities" (Genesis 19:25) = all truths separated from them, so that they had only falsities. "Cities" = doctrinal things, thus truths, which are said to be "overthrown," when there are falsities instead of truths...

@2456. "When God destroyed the cities of the plain" (Genesis 19:29) = when they perished through falsities of evil.

@2468[7]. They suffer themselves to imbue falsities, wherefore it is said, "the cities of Moab shall be for a desolation," and "they shall leave the cities, and dwell in the rocks" (Jeremiah 48:9, 28).

@2485. By the interior sight he was led by me through the cities where I had been... @SE 1933.

@2547[3]. "City against city" (Isaiah 19:2). "City" = what is doctrinal; here, what is heretical.

@2723[2]. Because the doctrine is thus made fit for human apprehension, the well Beersheba... is called "a city." "A city" = what is doctrinal in its complex.

@2826[5]. "A city" = doctrinal truth.

@2851[3]. The rational mind, from the goods and truths therein, is in the Word compared to "a city," and is called "a city"...

@--[6]. "A city" = the rational mind, or, what is the same, the goods and truths therein. References.

@--[7]. "The city of emptiness shall be broken" (Isaiah 24:10) = the human mind deprived of truth.

@2943. To "all that went in at the gate of his city" (Genesis 23:10) = as to the doctrinal things through which is faith... "City" = the truth which is of faith.

@--. In the Ancient Church, cities were not such cities as there were afterwards, that is, companies and congregations, but were cohabitations of separate families; the family of one parent constituted a city. Example(s). @4478.

@--. As nations and families represented the heavenly Societies, thus those things which are of love and charity, when a city is mentioned instead of the family, there is signified the truth which is of faith. Hence "the city -civitas- of God," and "the holy city -civitas-," in the genuine sense, = faith in the Lord; and as "a city," or "a city -civitas-" = faith, "the gate of a city" = doctrinal things, because these introduce to faith.

@3052. To "the city of Nahor" (Genesis 24:10) = cognate doctrinal things. "A city" = what is doctrinal.

@3055. "Outside the city" (Genesis 24:11) = removal from doctrinal things.

@3066. "The men of the city" (Genesis 24:13) = truths.

@--. The inhabitants of a city are in the Word sometimes called "the men of the city," sometimes "the inhabitants of the city;" when they are called "the men of the city," truths are signified; when "the inhabitants," goods are signified.

@3077. "Rebekah came out" (Genesis 24:15) = the affection of truth from doctrinal things... For she came out of the city, and by "a city" are signified doctrinal things.

@3216. When the Angels are conversing about the doctrinal things of charity and of faith, there sometimes appears in the lower sphere, where there is a corresponding Society of Spirits, the idea of a city, or of cities, with palaces therein... Hence it is evident what is signified by the cities seen by the prophets...

@3322[3]. "A city" = what is doctrinal.

@3466. "The name of the city Beersheba" (Genesis 26:33) = the quality of the doctrine thence... "City" = doctrine.

@3708[5]. Of those who are in ignorance of both good and truth, it is said that "they found no city of habitation" (Psalms 107:4).

@3730. "City" = what is doctrinal of truth.

@4169[2]. "The cities of the Samaritans" (Matthew 10:5) = those who are in falsities.

@4396. "He encamped at the face of the city" (Genesis 33:18) = application to the goods of that truth. "City" = truth.

@4478. "The men of the city" (Genesis 34:20) = those who are in truths of doctrine.

@4500. "They came upon the city confidently, and killed every male" (Genesis 34:25) = that they extirpated the truths of doctrine of the Church with the ancients. "City" = the doctrine which is of the Church. @4503.

@4507. "They took whatever was in the city, and whatever was in the field" (Genesis 34:28) = all the truth and good of the Church. "City" = what is doctrinal, thus the truth of the Church.

@4555. "The terror of God was upon the cities that were round about them" (Genesis 35:5) = that falsities and evils could not approach... "The cities round about them" = falsities and evils; for in the genuine sense, "cities" = truths of doctrine; and in the opposite, falsities of doctrine. The reason evils are also signified here by "city" is that the inhabitants also are understood.

@4581[9]. To "burn the city" (Jeremiah 32:29) = to destroy and vastate those who are in doctrinal things of falsity.

@4926[5]. "The breaches of the city of David" (Isaiah 22:9) = falsities of doctrine.

@5117[7]. To "build the waste cities" (Amos 9:14) = to rectify the falsified doctrinal things of truth.

@5135[9]. "The city through which they are said to run to and fro" (Joel 2:9) = doctrinal things of truth.

@5297. "Food in the cities" (Genesis 41:35) = such things in the interiors of the natural mind... "Cities" = the interiors of the natural mind. In the universal sense, "cities" = the doctrinal things of the Church (References); but in the singular sense, they = the interiors of man, where doctrinal things are, or rather where truths are conjoined with good. The truths and goods with man form as it were a city -civitatem-. Explained, Illustrated.

@5342. "He laid up the food in the cities" (Genesis 41:48) = in the interiors, namely, truths adjoined to good. "Cities" = the interiors of the natural mind.

@5774. "They laded every man upon his donkey, and returned to the city" (Genesis 44:13) = that from sensuous things truths were brought back into scientifics... "City" = doctrinal truth.

@6015[4]. "The city, and them that dwell therein" (Jeremiah 47:2) = the truth of the city, and thence good. @6297.

@6146. "He removed that people to cities" (Genesis 47:21) = that scientific truths were referred to doctrinal things... "Cities" = doctrinal things.

@6200[end]. When I thought of any city... the Spirits knew in a moment all things I had seen there...

