@392[10]. "As a city which coheres together with itself" (Psalms 122:3) = the doctrine in which all things are in order.

@410[7]. "The multitude of the city" (Isaiah 32:14) = all the truths of doctrine.

@417[10]. "Fortified cities" (Zephaniah 1:16) = false doctrinal things which they have confirmed.

@431[8]. "Jerusalem," here, = the Church as to doctrine, which is said to be built as a city which coheres together with itself when all things of its doctrine are in agreement and are unanimous, and when they mutually regard the Lord and love to Him from Him as the beginning and the end. It is said "built as a city," because "a city" = doctrine.

@449[5]. "The cities of Judah" (Jeremiah 17:26) = the truths of good.

@518[26]. "The city of God" (Psalms 46:4) = the Church as to doctrine.

@532[8]. As then they who, from spiritual affection, long for truth, will not find any truth in doctrines, wherever they seek for it, it is said, "two or three cities wandered unto one city to drink water, but they were not satisfied"; "two or three cities" = those who are in the affection of truth from good; "a city" = the truth of doctrine.

@538[4]. "The cities of Judah" (Isaiah 44:26) = the goods and truths of doctrine; the restoration of the Church and of doctrine is signified by their being inhabited and built.

@556[12]. "Emptiness of teeth in the cities" (Amos 4:6) = poverty of truth in doctrines.

@600[12]. "The desolate cities which the nations shall cause to be inhabited" (Isaiah 54:3) = truths from the goods of life; "desolate cities" = the truths of doctrine where before there were no truths.

@601[12]. "His cities are burned so that there is no inhabitant" (Jeremiah 2:15) = the destruction of the doctrinal things of the Church by evils, until there is no good of the Church remaining.

@612[3]. "The cities of Judah, to which it is said, Behold your God! the Lord Jehovih will come in strength" (Isaiah 40:9) = doctrinal things from the Word; "cities," doctrinal things; and "Judah," the Word.

@617[13]. "The cities great and good which shall be given them" (Deuteronomy 6:10) = doctrinal things from genuine goods and truths.

@638[14]. "Cities great and good" = doctrinal things which teach the goods of love and of charity.

@650[64]. "The violence of the land, of the city, and of all that dwell therein" (Habakkuk 2:17) = force brought to bear by falsities upon the truths and goods of the Church, and on its doctrine from the Word.

@652. "Their bodies shall lie upon the street of the great city" (Revelation 11:8) = the extinction by evils and falsities of doctrine... "A city" = doctrine.

