@--[7]. "The city of emptiness" (Isaiah 24:10) = the doctrine in which there is no truth, but falsity.

@--[8]. "The city of glory" (Jeremiah 49:25) = the doctrine of Divine truth; "the city of joy," the delight from the affection of good and truth there.

@--[9]. "City" (Ezekiel 11:6) = the doctrine of truth.

@--[11]. "The cities which will be devastated, so that there is no man, or inhabitant" (Zephaniah 3:6) = doctrinal things.

@--[13]. "According to the number of thy cities were thy gods, Judah" (Jeremiah 11:13) = as many falsities as doctrinal things.

@655[9]. To "persecute them from city to city" = that from one false doctrine they will wander into another.

@659[13]. "The holy city" was Zion and Jerusalem; but by these was meant Heaven...

